{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"4e98e0fa-fe84-485c-95b7-50a28a52364f","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have updated [deploy.sh](file:///tmp/h-LlMNxX/deploy.sh) and documented the changes and rationale in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-LlMNxX/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes:\n1. **Removed Stale Files from `site/` Without Dropping Live Pages**:\n   - Added `--delete` to `sync_site()`.\n   - Added `--exclude 's/*'` and `--exclude 'a/*'` to the site sync so that prerendered notes and author pages in S3 are not deleted before they can be updated.\n2. **Removed Stale / Private Pages Post-Upload**:\n   - Kept the `aws s3 cp` upload loop to ensure extensionless pages keep their `text/html; charset=utf-8` header and overwrite in-place without downtime.\n   - Added `aws s3 sync \"$ROOT/.build/pages/s/\" \"s3://$BUCKET/s/\" --delete --only-show-errors` and `aws s3 sync \"$ROOT/.build/pages/a/\" \"s3://$BUCKET/a/\" --delete --only-show-errors` after the upload step to remove any note or author pages no longer produced by the build.\n3. **Colleague's Note**:\n   - Documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-LlMNxX/ANSWER.md) which parts applied (excluding generated prefixes during main sync, in-place overwrite during upload, removing stale keys post-upload via `sync ... --delete`, and adding `--delete` to `site/` sync) and which parts were ignored or adapted (worklore-specific prefixes like `paths/` and the alternative `s3api list-objects-v2` manual cleanup).\n","duration_seconds":197.177419,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":327706,"output_tokens":7386,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":800737,"total_tokens":335092}}}
